<article class="env-lemma" id="0CNI">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CNI">Lemma <span data-tag="0CNI">32.3.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $I$ be a set and for each $i \in I$ let $f_ i : T_ i \to S$ be an affine morphism. Then the product $T = \prod T_ i$ exists in the category of schemes over $S$. In fact, we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{\{ i_1, \ldots , i_ n\}  \subset I} T_{i_1} \times _ S \ldots \times _ S T_{i_ n}  \]
</div>
  <p> and the projection morphisms $T \to T_{i_1} \times _ S \ldots \times _ S T_{i_ n}$ are affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: Argue as in the discussion preceding the lemma and use Lemma <a href="/tag/01YX" data-tag="01YX">32.2.2</a> for existence of the limit. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>